[
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-alas-and-did-my-saviour-bleed",
    "stanza_index": 1,
    "en": "Alas! and did my Saviour bleed, and did my Sovereign die?",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/alas_and_did_my_savior_bleed",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "watts_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-alas-and-did-my-saviour-bleed",
    "stanza_index": 2,
    "en": "Was it for crimes that I had done He groaned upon the tree?",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/alas_and_did_my_savior_bleed",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "watts_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-alas-and-did-my-saviour-bleed",
    "stanza_index": 3,
    "en": "Well might the sun in darkness hide, and shut his glories in,",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/alas_and_did_my_savior_bleed",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "watts_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-alas-and-did-my-saviour-bleed",
    "stanza_index": 4,
    "en": "But drops of grief can ne'er repay the debt of love I owe:",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/alas_and_did_my_savior_bleed",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "watts_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-when-i-survey-the-wondrous-cross",
    "stanza_index": 1,
    "en": "When I survey the wondrous cross on which the Prince of glory died,",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/when_i_survey_the_wondrous_cross_watts",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "watts_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-when-i-survey-the-wondrous-cross",
    "stanza_index": 2,
    "en": "Forbid it, Lord, that I should boast, save in the death of Christ my God;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/when_i_survey_the_wondrous_cross_watts",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "watts_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-when-i-survey-the-wondrous-cross",
    "stanza_index": 3,
    "en": "See, from His head, His hands, His feet, sorrow and love flow mingled down;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/when_i_survey_the_wondrous_cross_watts",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "watts_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-when-i-survey-the-wondrous-cross",
    "stanza_index": 4,
    "en": "Were the whole realm of nature mine, that were a present far too small;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/when_i_survey_the_wondrous_cross_watts",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "watts_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-there-is-a-fountain-filled-with-blood",
    "stanza_index": 1,
    "en": "There is a fountain filled with blood drawn from Immanuel's veins;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/there_is_a_fountain_filled_with_blood",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "cowper_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-there-is-a-fountain-filled-with-blood",
    "stanza_index": 2,
    "en": "The dying thief rejoiced to see that fountain in his day;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/there_is_a_fountain_filled_with_blood",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "cowper_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-there-is-a-fountain-filled-with-blood",
    "stanza_index": 3,
    "en": "Dear dying Lamb, Thy precious blood shall never lose its power,",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/there_is_a_fountain_filled_with_blood",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "cowper_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-there-is-a-fountain-filled-with-blood",
    "stanza_index": 4,
    "en": "E'er since by faith I saw the stream Thy flowing wounds supply,",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/there_is_a_fountain_filled_with_blood",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "cowper_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-how-sweet-the-name-of-jesus-sounds",
    "stanza_index": 1,
    "en": "How sweet the Name of Jesus sounds in a believer's ear!",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/how_sweet_the_name_of_jesus_sounds",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "newton_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-how-sweet-the-name-of-jesus-sounds",
    "stanza_index": 2,
    "en": "It makes the wounded spirit whole, and calms the troubled breast;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/how_sweet_the_name_of_jesus_sounds",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "newton_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-how-sweet-the-name-of-jesus-sounds",
    "stanza_index": 3,
    "en": "Dear Name! the rock on which I build, my shield and hiding place,",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/how_sweet_the_name_of_jesus_sounds",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "newton_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-how-sweet-the-name-of-jesus-sounds",
    "stanza_index": 4,
    "en": "Jesus, my Shepherd, Husband, Friend, my Prophet, Priest, and King,",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/how_sweet_the_name_of_jesus_sounds",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "newton_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-amazing-grace",
    "stanza_index": 1,
    "en": "Amazing grace! how sweet the sound that saved a wretch like me!",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/amazing_grace_how_sweet_the_sound",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "newton_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-amazing-grace",
    "stanza_index": 2,
    "en": "Twas grace that taught my heart to fear, and grace my fears relieved;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/amazing_grace_how_sweet_the_sound",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "newton_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-amazing-grace",
    "stanza_index": 3,
    "en": "Through many dangers, toils, and snares, I have already come;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/amazing_grace_how_sweet_the_sound",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "newton_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-amazing-grace",
    "stanza_index": 4,
    "en": "The Lord has promised good to me, His word my hope secures;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/amazing_grace_how_sweet_the_sound",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "newton_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-all-hail-the-power-of-jesus-name",
    "stanza_index": 1,
    "en": "All hail the power of Jesus' name! Let angels prostrate fall;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/all_hail_the_power_of_jesus_name",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "perronet_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-all-hail-the-power-of-jesus-name",
    "stanza_index": 2,
    "en": "Ye chosen seed of Israel's race, ye ransomed from the fall,",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/all_hail_the_power_of_jesus_name",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "perronet_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-all-hail-the-power-of-jesus-name",
    "stanza_index": 3,
    "en": "Let every kindred, every tribe, on this terrestrial ball,",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/all_hail_the_power_of_jesus_name",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "perronet_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-all-hail-the-power-of-jesus-name",
    "stanza_index": 4,
    "en": "O that with yonder sacred throng we at His feet may fall!",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/all_hail_the_power_of_jesus_name",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "perronet_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-holy-holy-holy",
    "stanza_index": 1,
    "en": "Holy, holy, holy! Lord God Almighty! Early in the morning our song shall rise to Thee;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/holy_holy_holy_lord_god_almighty",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "heber_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-holy-holy-holy",
    "stanza_index": 2,
    "en": "Holy, holy, holy! all the saints adore Thee, casting down their golden crowns around the glassy sea;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/holy_holy_holy_lord_god_almighty",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "heber_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-holy-holy-holy",
    "stanza_index": 3,
    "en": "Holy, holy, holy! though the darkness hide Thee, though the eye of sinful man Thy glory may not see;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/holy_holy_holy_lord_god_almighty",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "heber_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-holy-holy-holy",
    "stanza_index": 4,
    "en": "Holy, holy, holy! Lord God Almighty! All Thy works shall praise Thy name in earth and sky and sea;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/holy_holy_holy_lord_god_almighty",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "heber_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-abide-with-me",
    "stanza_index": 1,
    "en": "Abide with me: fast falls the eventide; the darkness deepens; Lord, with me abide.",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/abide_with_me_fast_falls_the_eventide",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "lyte_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-abide-with-me",
    "stanza_index": 2,
    "en": "Swift to its close ebbs out life's little day; earth's joys grow dim, its glories pass away;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/abide_with_me_fast_falls_the_eventide",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "lyte_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-abide-with-me",
    "stanza_index": 3,
    "en": "I need Thy presence every passing hour; what but Thy grace can foil the tempter's power?",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/abide_with_me_fast_falls_the_eventide",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "lyte_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-abide-with-me",
    "stanza_index": 4,
    "en": "Hold Thou Thy cross before my closing eyes; shine through the gloom, and point me to the skies;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/abide_with_me_fast_falls_the_eventide",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "lyte_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-rock-of-ages",
    "stanza_index": 1,
    "en": "Rock of Ages, cleft for me, let me hide myself in Thee;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/rock_of_ages_cleft_for_me_let",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "toplady_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-rock-of-ages",
    "stanza_index": 2,
    "en": "Not the labors of my hands can fulfill Thy law's demands;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/rock_of_ages_cleft_for_me_let",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "toplady_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-rock-of-ages",
    "stanza_index": 3,
    "en": "Nothing in my hand I bring, simply to Thy cross I cling;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/rock_of_ages_cleft_for_me_let",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "toplady_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-rock-of-ages",
    "stanza_index": 4,
    "en": "While I draw this fleeting breath, when my eyes shall close in death,",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/rock_of_ages_cleft_for_me_let",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "toplady_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-just-as-i-am",
    "stanza_index": 1,
    "en": "Just as I am, without one plea, but that Thy blood was shed for me,",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/just_as_i_am_without_one_plea",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "elliott_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-just-as-i-am",
    "stanza_index": 2,
    "en": "Just as I am, and waiting not to rid my soul of one dark blot,",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/just_as_i_am_without_one_plea",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "elliott_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-just-as-i-am",
    "stanza_index": 3,
    "en": "Just as I am, though tossed about with many a conflict, many a doubt,",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/just_as_i_am_without_one_plea",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "elliott_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-just-as-i-am",
    "stanza_index": 4,
    "en": "Just as I am, Thou wilt receive, wilt welcome, pardon, cleanse, relieve;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/just_as_i_am_without_one_plea",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "elliott_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-when-i-see-the-blood",
    "stanza_index": 1,
    "en": "Christ our Redeemer died on the cross, died for the sinner, paid all his due;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/christ_our_redeemer_died_on_the_cross",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "foote_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-when-i-see-the-blood",
    "stanza_index": 2,
    "en": "Chiefest of sinners, Jesus will save; all He has promised, that He will do;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/christ_our_redeemer_died_on_the_cross",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "foote_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-when-i-see-the-blood",
    "stanza_index": 3,
    "en": "Judgment is coming, all will be there, who have rejected, who have refused;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/christ_our_redeemer_died_on_the_cross",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "foote_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-when-i-see-the-blood",
    "stanza_index": 4,
    "en": "O what a Saviour, that He died for me! From condemnation He hath made me free;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/christ_our_redeemer_died_on_the_cross",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "foote_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-a-debtor-to-mercy-alone",
    "stanza_index": 1,
    "en": "A debtor to mercy alone, of covenant mercy I sing;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/a_debtor_to_mercy_alone",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "toplady_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-a-debtor-to-mercy-alone",
    "stanza_index": 2,
    "en": "The work which His goodness began, the arm of His strength will complete;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/a_debtor_to_mercy_alone",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "toplady_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-a-debtor-to-mercy-alone",
    "stanza_index": 3,
    "en": "My name from the palms of His hands eternity will not erase;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/a_debtor_to_mercy_alone",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "toplady_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-a-mind-at-perfect-peace",
    "stanza_index": 1,
    "en": "A mind at perfect peace with God: O what a word is this!",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/a_mind_at_perfect_peace_with_god",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "paget_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-a-mind-at-perfect-peace",
    "stanza_index": 2,
    "en": "By nature and by practice far, how very far from God!",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/a_mind_at_perfect_peace_with_god",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "paget_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-a-mind-at-perfect-peace",
    "stanza_index": 3,
    "en": "So near, so very near to God, I cannot nearer be;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/a_mind_at_perfect_peace_with_god",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "paget_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-according-to-thy-gracious-word",
    "stanza_index": 1,
    "en": "According to Thy gracious word, in meek humility,",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/according_to_thy_gracious_word",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "montgomery_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-according-to-thy-gracious-word",
    "stanza_index": 2,
    "en": "Thy body broken for my sake, my bread from heaven shall be;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/according_to_thy_gracious_word",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "montgomery_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-according-to-thy-gracious-word",
    "stanza_index": 3,
    "en": "Gethsemane can I forget? Or there Thy conflict see,",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/according_to_thy_gracious_word",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "montgomery_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-according-to-thy-gracious-word",
    "stanza_index": 4,
    "en": "When to the cross I turn my eyes, and rest on Calvary,",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/according_to_thy_gracious_word",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "montgomery_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "bhb-classic-023",
    "stanza_index": 1,
    "en": "Beneath the cross of Jesus I fain would take my stand,",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/beneath_the_cross_of_jesus",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "clephane_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "bhb-classic-023",
    "stanza_index": 2,
    "en": "O safe and happy shelter! O refuge tried and sweet!",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/beneath_the_cross_of_jesus",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "clephane_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "bhb-classic-023",
    "stanza_index": 3,
    "en": "Upon that cross of Jesus mine eye at times can see",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/beneath_the_cross_of_jesus",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "clephane_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "bhb-classic-023",
    "stanza_index": 4,
    "en": "I take, O cross, thy shadow for my abiding place;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/beneath_the_cross_of_jesus",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "clephane_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-how-firm-a-foundation",
    "stanza_index": 1,
    "en": "How firm a foundation, ye saints of the Lord, is laid for your faith in His excellent word!",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/how_firm_a_foundation_ye_saints_of",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "rippon_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-how-firm-a-foundation",
    "stanza_index": 2,
    "en": "Fear not, I am with thee, O be not dismayed, for I am thy God, and will still give thee aid;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/how_firm_a_foundation_ye_saints_of",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "rippon_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-how-firm-a-foundation",
    "stanza_index": 3,
    "en": "When through the deep waters I call thee to go, the rivers of sorrow shall not overflow;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/how_firm_a_foundation_ye_saints_of",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "rippon_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-how-firm-a-foundation",
    "stanza_index": 4,
    "en": "The soul that on Jesus hath leaned for repose I will not, I will not desert to his foes;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/how_firm_a_foundation_ye_saints_of",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "rippon_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-o-god-our-help-in-ages-past",
    "stanza_index": 1,
    "en": "O God, our help in ages past, our hope for years to come,",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/o_god_our_help_in_ages_past",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "watts_pd"
  },
  {
    "hymn_id": "pd-o-god-our-help-in-ages-past",
    "stanza_index": 2,
    "en": "Under the shadow of Thy throne Thy saints have dwelt secure;",
    "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/o_god_our_help_in_ages_past",
    "license": "public_domain",
    "en_source": "watts_pd"
  },
  {
